{"name":"Air Superiority Blue","hex":"#72a0c1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"air","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Airoran."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance constituting Earth's atmosphere: a gaseous mixture of nitrogen, oxygen, and various trace gases.","The substance of the atmosphere seen as an agency of freshness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air"},{"term":"superiority","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being superior.","The right which the superior enjoys in the land held by the vassal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superiority"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Air Force blue","blocks":[{"text":"Air Force blue colours are a variety of colours that are mostly various tones of the colour azure, the purest tones of which are identified as being the colour of the sky on a clear day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg/330px-RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_Force_blue"},{"title":"Air supremacy","blocks":[{"text":"Air supremacy is the degree to which a side in a conflict holds control of air power over opposing forces. There are levels of control of the air in aerial warfare. Control of the air is the aerial equivalent of command of the sea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/384th_Bomb_Group_8th_AF_B-17_Bombers_in_Formation_Over_Clouds.2.jpg/330px-384th_Bomb_Group_8th_AF_B-17_Bombers_in_Formation_Over_Clouds.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_supremacy"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg/500px-RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg/1280px-RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg/500px-RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thornycroft Antar Mk 3 in Royal Air Force blue col